# Lead-lens sign-off — cli#477 init banner collapse
- date: 2026-11-06
- branch: fix/init-banner-collapse
- lead: edward-tufte

## Findings cleared

- T1, T2, T3 (aggregation depth + key shape) — cleared. Depth rule is one
  level, two under .claude/. Two tests pin it: group count under 30, and no
  group key ending in a file extension.
- N4, N5 (actionable facts stay visible and name their flag) — cleared.
- F6, F7, F8 (characterization moved not weakened; manifest coverage added;
  test totals compared) — cleared.

No red findings. One amber raised and closed during the work: the first
grouping rule used two levels everywhere and produced 27 group lines, with
standards/ split into eleven. Reduced to one level outside .claude/, which
gave 14. Measured, not estimated.

## Verification performed

- Real run, fresh target: 201 stdout lines before, 44 after. Inventory is 14
  lines of the 44.
- --verbose run: 204 lines; every pattern the characterization test pins still
  present, in order.
- --json: schema_version 3, totals.files 554, refused 0. Unchanged.
- --dry-run: unchanged.
- Full suite: 63 files, 551 tests, 0 failed.

## Second pass — 2026-11-07

Operator asked whether 44 lines was still too many. It was. The 14-line
directory summary was inventory one grain coarser, and a reader cannot act
on "standards: 102 files" either. Banner is now 4 lines on a clean install.

- Dropped by default, kept under --verbose: the directory summary, the
  statusline note on a clean install.
- Kept after reverting a gate: "N config files created". On a partial
  install it is the only evidence substrate.config.md landed, which
  tests/init.test.ts "partial state" asserts. Changing that test to fit a
  line budget would have been weakening it; the budget allowed the line.
- Left alone, named: "1 config files created" should read "file". Two tests
  pin the plural spelling, so the fix is its own change.

## Findings cleared — second pass

- Three tests failed on the first run of this pass. Two were my own, written
  for the 14-line design and stale within the same session; rewritten to
  assert the new contract, not weakened to pass. One was init.test.ts
  "partial state", a real adopter concern; the source changed, not the test.
- Test total read 549 against a 551 baseline while 4 tests were added. Chased
  per the green-count-with-smaller-total discipline rather than accepted.
  Cause: the 551 baseline ran on feat/brass-mark, where
  tests/init-brand-mark.test.ts carries 17 tests; this branch is off
  origin/main, where it carries 11. 551 - 6 + 2 + 2 = 549. Verified with
  `git show feat/brass-mark:tests/init-brand-mark.test.ts`. Nothing absent.

## CTA line (cli#477)

Added one line to src/lib/init-value-test-block.ts, the Sam-verbatim block.
The block walks the reader to /build, and /build opens a pull request. A pull
request needs a GitHub remote, which init does not create, so today the
reader finds out at step three. The line names the requirement rather than
naming /onboard-repo, because that skill's Path A requires bassclef cloned
as a peer at ~/src/<org>/bassclef — which an npm adopter does not have.

Needs bassclef-upstream#2006 updated per the note in that file. Two tickets
filed separately: Path C unwritten, and the Path A peer-clone prereq.
